  "problem": "A teacher of a group of $4$ students wants to check the strength of the linear correlation between $x,$ the number of hours the students had slept the night before an exam, and $y,$ the student's score in the exam. The data is shown below. \n\n| **Number of hours** | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Score ** | $56$ | $68$ | $81$ | $79$ |\n\nYou are given that the means are $\\overset{―}{x}=5$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=71.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\rho ≈0.81$\n\nII. There is a strong positive correlation between $x$ and $y.$\n\nIII. There is a weak positive correlation between $x$ and $y.$\n\n*Hint: $|\\rho |>0.7$ indicates a strong correlation, and $0.3\\le |\\rho |\\le 0.7$ indicates a weak correlation.*",
